:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.4.5 構成比の分母と合計を確認する</h3>","<h3>部分集計を明細の全体合計と照合する</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.4.6 集計・保存・再読込を照合する</h3>","<h3>二つのCSVを保存後に再読込する</h3>":"<h4>用途別CSVを保存し、再読込して検証する</h4>","<h3>例題から応用へ</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.4.7 集計と順位を別の判断へ応用する</h3>"}},"en":{"Lesson 3.1: Tabular data, CSV, and pandas":{"<h2>Treat a collection of records as an inspectable table</h2>":"<h2>Treat a collection of records as an inspectable table</h2><h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.1.1 Tabular data — rows, columns, and cells</h3>","<h3>Align one observation per row and one variable per column</h3>":"<h4>Align one observation per row and one variable per column</h4>","<h3>CSV is a text representation of a table</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.1.2 CSV — a text format for exchanging tables</h3>","<h3>A relative path is interpreted from the current working directory</h3>":"<h4>Relative paths and the file actually loaded</h4>","<h3>Express read_csv assumptions in code</h3>":"<h4>Express read_csv assumptions in code</h4>","<h3>Inspect shape, names, types, and missingness before calculation</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.1.3 pandas — load and inspect a DataFrame</h3>","<h3>One column is a Series; a multi-column table is a DataFrame</h3>":"<h4>Display every row and count raw category values</h4><p><code>head()</code> is useful for a first sample, but a person inspecting a 37-row source can use <code>to_string(index=False)</code> to prevent middle rows from being replaced by an ellipsis. Before correcting a category column, inspect its raw values and counts. <code>value_counts(dropna=False, sort=False)</code> includes missingness and retains first-appearance order. Convert the Series to a two-column table when the result needs named fields.</p><pre style=\"background:#f4f5f7;border:1px solid #d8dce1;padding:1em;overflow:auto\"><code>print(df.to_string(index=False, line_width=200))\n\ndistrict_counts = (\n    df[&quot;district&quot;]\n    .value_counts(dropna=False, sort=False)\n    .rename_axis(&quot;district&quot;)\n    .reset_index(name=&quot;records&quot;)\n)\nprint(district_counts.to_string(index=False, formatters={&quot;district&quot;: repr}))</code></pre><h4>One column is a Series; multiple columns form a DataFrame</h4>","<h3>Add derived columns only after inspection</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.1.4 pandas — column calculations and CSV output</h3>","<h3>Distinguish the index from an operational identifier</h3>":"<h4>Distinguish the index from an operational identifier</h4>","<h3>Diagnose loading failures by cause</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.1.5 Diagnose loading problems by cause</h3>","<h3>From guided example to transfer</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.1.6 Transfer the example to another table</h3>"},"Lesson 3.2: Data selection, filtering, and Boolean logic":{"<h2>Translate an analysis question into displayed columns and row conditions</h2>":"<h2>Translate an analysis question into displayed columns and row conditions</h2><h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.2.1 Separate a question into displayed columns and row conditions</h3>","<h3>Separate displayed columns from partial conditions</h3>":"<h4>Validate required columns and separate partial conditions</h4>","<h3>Select needed fields with a list of column names</h3>":"<h4>Select the fields needed for the result</h4>","<h3>loc uses labels; iloc uses positions</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.2.2 Select rows and columns with loc and iloc</h3>","<h3>A comparison creates one True/False value per row</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.2.3 Turn comparisons into Boolean masks</h3>","<h3>Use & | ~ and parentheses for pandas conditions</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.2.4 Build compound conditions with Boolean logic</h3>","<h3>Verify AND, OR, and NOT through counts</h3>":"<h4>Verify AND, OR, and NOT through counts</h4>","<h3>Use isin for membership and between for a range</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.2.5 Express membership, ranges, and missingness</h3>","<h3>Make missingness explicit instead of losing rows accidentally</h3>":"<h4>Do not lose missing rows accidentally</h4>","<h3>Combine named masks in loc</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.2.6 Filter with masks and verify row counts</h3>","<h3>A Boolean mask aligns by index label</h3>":"<h4>Align masks and rows by index label</h4>","<h3>From guided example to transfer</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.2.7 Transfer the conditions to another question</h3>"},"Lesson 3.3: Data cleaning and audit records":{"<h2>Define the problem before changing the data</h2>":"<h2>Define the problem before changing the data</h2><h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.3.1 Preserve the source and define quality problems</h3>","<h3>Profile types, missingness, categories, and ranges before correction</h3>":"<h4>Inspect types, missingness, categories, and ranges first</h4>","<h3>Separate source, working, and analysis-ready data</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.3.2 Separate source, working, and analysis-ready data</h3>","<h3>Distinguish conversion failure from source missingness</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.3.3 Separate type conversion from missingness</h3>","<h3>Missing does not mean zero</h3>":"<h4>Do not confuse missingness with zero</h4>","<h3>Normalise labels without discarding source text</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.3.4 Normalise labels while retaining source values</h3>","<h3>Test individual ranges and cross-field relationships separately</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.3.5 Test ranges, cross-field constraints, and duplicates</h3>","<h3>Define a business key before checking duplicates</h3>":"<h4>Use a business key to flag every duplicate row</h4>","<h3>Separate detection from action</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.3.6 Build a verification table from quality flags</h3>","<h3>Build a row-level verification report from individual flags</h3>":"<h4>Preserve row-level reasons in the verification report</h4>","<h3>Make the workflow reproducible with an audit record and assertions</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.3.7 Record the audit and validate again</h3>","<h3>Boundary rules before the project</h3>":"<h4>Validate boundary cases before the project</h4>","<h3>From worked example to transfer</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.3.8 Transfer quality rules to another dataset</h3>"},"Lesson 3.4: Grouping and summary statistics":{"<h2>Define what one result row means before aggregation</h2>":"<h2>Define what one result row means before aggregation</h2><h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.4.1 Define the grain of detail and summary rows</h3>","<h3>groupby splits, applies, and combines</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.4.2 Split, count, and combine with groupby</h3>","<h3>Distinguish size, count, and nunique</h3>":"<h4>Distinguish what size, count, and nunique count</h4>","<h3>Put a conditional count into named aggregation</h3>":"<h4>Put a conditional count into named aggregation</h4>","<h3>Totals, centre, and spread answer different questions</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.4.3 Calculate summary statistics and rates</h3>","<h3>Aggregate compatible numerators and denominators before a rate</h3>":"<h4>Calculate rates from compatible aggregate totals</h4>","<h3>Make ranking deterministic with mixed sort directions</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.4.4 Build reproducible rankings from multiple conditions</h3>","<h3>Multiple keys preserve hierarchy</h3>":"<h4>Preserve comparison hierarchy with multiple keys</h4>","<h3>State the proportion denominator and check 100%</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.4.5 Check the denominator and 100% total of proportions</h3>","<h3>Reconcile grouped totals with detail</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.4.6 Reconcile aggregation, saving, and re-reading</h3>","<h3>Re-read two CSV products after saving</h3>":"<h4>Save purpose-specific CSVs and validate them after re-reading</h4>","<h3>From worked example to transfer</h3>":"<h3 style=\"margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb\">3.4.7 Transfer aggregation and ranking to another decision</h3>"}}}
JSON, true, 512, JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR);
$results = [];
foreach ($all[$language] as $pagename => $replacements) {
    $page = $DB->get_record('page', ['course' => $course->id, 'name' => $pagename], '*', MUST_EXIST);
    if (!str_contains($page->content, 'PYAI-V36-CHAPTER3-TOPICS')) {
        foreach ($replacements as $old => $new) {
            $count = substr_count($page->content, $old);
            if ($count !== 1) throw new RuntimeException("$shortname $pagename expected one heading, found $count: $old");
            $page->content = str_replace($old, $new, $page->content);
        }
        if (str_contains($pagename, '3.4')) {
            $rankingText = strpos($page->content, '>3.4.4 ');
            $proportionText = strpos($page->content, '>3.4.5 ');
            $transferText = strpos($page->content, '>3.4.7 ');
            if ($rankingText === false || $proportionText === false || $transferText === false) {
                throw new RuntimeException("$shortname $pagename cannot locate 3.4 blocks");
            }
            $rankingStart = strrpos(substr($page->content, 0, $rankingText), '<h3 style=');
            $transferStart = strrpos(substr($page->content, 0, $transferText), '<h3 style=');
            if ($rankingStart > $proportionText) {
                $rankingBlock = substr($page->content, $rankingStart, $transferStart - $rankingStart);
                $page->content = substr_replace($page->content, '', $rankingStart, $transferStart - $rankingStart);
                $proportionText = strpos($page->content, '>3.4.5 ');
                $proportionStart = strrpos(substr($page->content, 0, $proportionText), '<h3 style=');
                $page->content = substr_replace($page->content, $rankingBlock, $proportionStart, 0);
            }
        }
        $count = substr_count($page->content, '</div>');
        if ($count !== 1) throw new RuntimeException("$shortname $pagename outer div count $count");
        $page->content = str_replace('</div>', '<p style="display:none">PYAI-V36-CHAPTER3-TOPICS</p></div>', $page->content);
        $page->timemodified = time();
        $DB->update_record('page', $page);
    }
    $results[] = ['course' => $shortname, 'page' => $pagename, 'topics' => substr_count($page->content, 'style="margin-top:2em;padding:.55em .75em;border-left:4px solid #0f6cbf;background:#f3f7fb')];
}
rebuild_course_cache($course->id, true);
echo json_encode($results, JSON_UNESCAPED_UNICODE | JSON_UNESCAPED_SLASHES), PHP_EOL;
